---

<Layout
  title="Teaching"
  description="Courses, assignments, courseware, and workshops taught or developed by Nim Dvir."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <h1>Teaching</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I teach undergraduate and graduate courses in information systems,
      business analytics, databases, and programming. I also advise student
      research and design projects.
    </p>
  </header>
  <section class="section" style="border-top:0;padding-top:0">
    <h2>Courses</h2>
    <p>
      My current teaching includes BITM 330 and Digital Citizenship. The lists
      below include earlier courses and course development, with dates for each.
    </p>
    <h3>Graduate and MBA</h3>
    <ul class="course-list">
      {graduate.map(([code, title, context]) => (
        <li>
          <p class="status-label">{code}</p>
          <strong>{title}</strong>
          <span>{context}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <h3>Undergraduate</h3>
    <ul class="course-list">
      {undergraduate.map(([code, title, context]) => (
        <li>
          {code && <p class="status-label">{code}</p>}
          <strong>{title}</strong>
          <span>{context}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <a href={cvUrl}>Full teaching history</a>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="courseware">
    <h2>Textbook and courseware</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <h3>Using Data to Drive Business Performance</h3>
      <p>
        I’m writing a textbook on databases, SQL, business analytics, and
        information systems. The companion website includes explanations,
        exercises, and quizzes used in BITM 330.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        The manuscript is under review with Cengage Learning, as reported in my
        September 2026 CV.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href="https://database-textbook.dimapublishing.com/">
        Open courseware ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="split-section">
    <h2>Assignments and student projects</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Students work on database queries, data analysis, user research, and
        prototypes. In the Business Analytics Practicum and graduate Field
        Study, teams work on questions from organizations and present their
        research and recommendations.
      </p>
      <p>
        The portfolio includes student projects I advised, including{" "}
        <a href="/projects/costco-mobile-app/">a shopping-app concept</a>,{" "}
        <a href="/projects/dexcom-g7-plus/">research on a diabetes app</a>, and{" "}
        <a href="/projects/barrier-free-living/">
          content recommendations for a nonprofit
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/projects/">
        View projects
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="split-section">
    <h2>Online teaching</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I’m developing the fully asynchronous BITM 330 course for UAlbany’s
        Online BSBA program. I’ve also taught BITM 522 and Digital Citizenship
        online.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="split-section">
    <h2>AI in coursework</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        My assignments include AI-assisted coding and evaluation of model
        outputs. Students are asked to explain their approach and assess the
        results they submit.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m also preparing{" "}
        <a href="/research/ai-pedagogy/">research on AI and student learning</a>
        , including AI-assisted summarization and academic advising.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="split-section">
    <h2>Workshops</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <h3>AI Agents in VS Code for Academic Work</h3>
      <p class="small">
        Cengage Computing Experience · October 21–23, 2026 · Fort Lauderdale,
        Florida
      </p>
      <p>
        This session covers files, project instructions, prompts, and using AI
        agents for academic work. The examples include building websites and
        reviewing changes.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button" href="https://nimdvir.github.io/cce-2026/">
          Session materials ↗
        </a>
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/nimdvir/cce-2026">
          GitHub repository ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
